# Target C — audited §152 linear defect from the pure triangular-tooth regime

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Lifecycle:** audited-working proof-only route module; theorem-state authority unchanged.  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** **STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.**

This module normalizes the live theorem from the older pure-tooth endpoint branch. The exact endpoint exclusion is only a special case; the useful statement is a uniform Type-II linear loss from the near-pure two-edge-tooth regime.

Let

- `q` be the number of loaded force-hull vertices;
- `m` be the number of nonunit loaded-hull sides;
- `T_triangle` be the total number of augmented triangular faces in the harmonic-cell graphs;
- `r_deep:=m-T_triangle>=0` be the number of nonunit loaded-hull intervals that are not exact two-edge teeth;
- `Q` be the global bounded-face degree excess;
- `f` be the number of bounded nonquadrilateral contact faces;
- `k=d_H+s_Z`; and
- `u_B>=0` be the Type-II extra outer-walk surplus.

For sufficiently large Type-II survivors,

\[
\boxed{
q-T_{\triangle}=e_{BB}+r_{deep}
=Q+2k+u_B+r_{deep}.
}
\tag{152.1}
\]

Consequently

\[
\boxed{
q-T_{\triangle}\ge f+2k.
}
\tag{152.2}
\]

Normalized audited-working §142 gives

\[
\liminf_{D\to\infty}{2f-k\over D}
\ge
\gamma,
\qquad
\gamma:=2\sqrt{\frac\pi{2\sqrt3}}-\frac\pi2
=0.333829286933018\ldots .
\tag{152.3}
\]

Combining (152.2) and (152.3),

\[
\boxed{
\liminf_{D\to\infty}{q-T_{\triangle}\over D}
\ge
\frac\gamma2
=
\sqrt{\frac\pi{2\sqrt3}}-\frac\pi4
=0.166914643466509\ldots .
}
\tag{152.4}
\]

More sharply, along any subsequence with `k/D -> kappa`,

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {q-T_{\triangle}\over D}
\ge
\frac\gamma2+\frac52\kappa.
}
\tag{152.5}
\]

Thus an unbounded Type-II C-II survivor sequence cannot satisfy

\[
T_{\triangle}=q-o(D).
\tag{152.6}
\]

At least `0.1669146434D-o(D)` loaded-hull positions are lost from the exact two-edge-tooth population, and the loss must be paid by the explicit currencies in (152.1): bounded-face degree excess, topology defect, outer-walk surplus, or deeper nonunit-hull detours.

---

## 152.1 Exact finite identity

The centralized Type-II loaded-contact theorem gives

\[
c_B=0,
\qquad
q-m=e_{BB}.
\tag{152.7}
\]

Normalized post-126 §130 identifies `T_triangle` exactly with the nonunit loaded-hull intervals whose distinguished outer contact route has occurrence length two. Therefore

\[
r_{deep}:=m-T_{\triangle}\ge0
\tag{152.8}
\]

and

\[
q-T_{\triangle}
=(q-m)+(m-T_{\triangle})
=e_{BB}+r_{deep}.
\tag{152.9}
\]

Canonical Section 63, after `c_B=0`, gives

\[
e_{BB}=Q+2k+u_B.
\tag{152.10}
\]

Substitution proves (152.1). Since every bounded nonquadrilateral face has degree at least five,

\[
Q\ge f,
\tag{152.11}
\]

which proves (152.2).

All quantities are occurrence-safe and no identification of tooth intervals with distinct apex vertices is used.

---

## 152.2 Insert the stopped-train phase gap

From §142,

\[
2f-k\ge(\gamma-o(1))D.
\]

Rewrite

\[
f={1\over2}(2f-k)+{1\over2}k.
\]

Then (152.2) gives

\[
\begin{aligned}
q-T_{\triangle}
&\ge f+2k\\
&={1\over2}(2f-k)+{5\over2}k\\
&\ge {\gamma\over2}D+{5\over2}k-o(D).
\end{aligned}
\]

This proves (152.4)–(152.5).

---

## 152.3 What the theorem excludes

The exact one-component all-two-edge-tooth endpoint is immediately impossible, but (152.4) is stronger: it excludes every asymptotically pure regime with only `o(D)` non-tooth positions.

The theorem does **not** show which one of the four currencies

\[
Q,
\qquad k,
\qquad u_B,
\qquad r_{deep}
\]

must be linear in a given survivor. It only forces their sum, with the exact coefficients in (152.1), to pay a linear deficit.

This is compatible with the current live frontier: linear bounded-face/corridor defect and linear outer-walk surplus remain possible, and neither has yet been converted into a same-cardinality strict diameter descent.

---

## 152.4 Scope

- §142 and the post-126 structural chain are audited-working proof-only inputs.
- The result is Type II only.
- No contact-isolated source point is removed, reclassified, or inserted into the core affine-kernel theorem.
- `T_triangle` is an interval/augmented-face count, not the number of distinct unloaded tooth apex vertices.
- No KKT coefficient floor, response hypothesis, or withdrawn Section-121 normalization is used.

**Disposition:** audited-working proof-only theorem. C-II and Level I remain open.
